inputs, not on the training set. Of the {{mechanism.q1.revival.n_revived:n}} Stage 2 runs whose last hidden layer reached
≥ 99 % dead, {{mechanism.q1.revival.n_revived}} later ended < 50 % dead (all CIFAR-10); {{mechanism.q1.revival.n_revived_reach15}} of them reach > 15 %
validation accuracy again and {{mechanism.q1.revival.n_revived_final_ge15}} end ≥ 15 %. Another {{mechanism.q1.revival.cifar10.revived_then_died_again.n:.0f}} CIFAR-10 runs revived
and died again; {{mechanism.q1.revival.cifar10.stayed_dead.n:.0f}} CIFAR-10 and {{mechanism.q1.revival.mnist.stayed_dead.n:.0f}} MNIST runs stayed dead. Revival
coincides with conv-weight change: median relative conv-weight change per epoch while dead
{{mechanism.q1.revival.dw_conv_median_revived:.3f}} in revived runs vs {{mechanism.q1.revival.dw_conv_median_not_revived:.4f}} in the others; the conv dw is zero in
{{mechanism.q1.revival.n_dw_conv_zero_revived}} revived and {{mechanism.q1.revival.n_dw_conv_zero_not_revived}} non-revived runs. Non-zero updates below a "dead" layer mean that
some of its units still fire on training inputs.

**Q2. Hybrid.** Stage 0 mlp2 H128 [E-S0]: the ReLU half of hidden2 is {{mechanism.q2.s0_h128_lr0.03.hybrid_relu_dead_hidden2:.3f}} dead (median) at
LR 0.03 and {{mechanism.q2.s0_h128_lr0.05.hybrid_relu_dead_hidden2:.2f}} at LR 0.05, where the tanh half (saturated fraction
{{mechanism.q2.s0_h128_lr0.05.hybrid_tanh_sat_hidden2:.3f}}) carries the network. Stage 2 CNN at LR 0.02 [D]: on MNIST the hybrid is
"protected" (ReLU half < 50 % dead) in {{report.q2.mnist_cnn_lr0.02.protected}} runs; on CIFAR-10 it is "carried" (ReLU half ≥ 50 %
dead, final ≥ 15 %) in {{report.q2.cifar10_cnn_lr0.02.carried}}, protected in {{report.q2.cifar10_cnn_lr0.02.protected}} and failed in {{report.q2.cifar10_cnn_lr0.02.failed}}. The
switch from protected to carried happens at LR {{mechanism.q2.switch.s2_mnist_cfg1_h128_tanh+relu:lr}} on MNIST cfg1 H128 and at LR
{{mechanism.q2.switch.s2_cifar10_cfg1_h128_tanh+relu:lr}} on CIFAR-10 cfg1 H128 (`q2_regime_switch.csv`).

**Q3. Mask placement (correlational).** Stage 2 cfg2 H 128/256, failing runs: the hidden layer's
ReLU units reach 50 % dead first in {{report.q3.cifar10.relu.hidden_first}} CIFAR-10 ReLU failures and
{{report.q3.cifar10.tanh+relu@hidden.hidden_first}} @hidden failures. At CIFAR-10 H128 LR 0.02 [D], final hidden-layer ReLU dead
fraction: ReLU {{mechanism.q3.cifar10_h128_lr0.02.relu.hidden_relu_dead:.3f}}, @hidden {{mechanism.q3.cifar10_h128_lr0.02.tanh+relu@hidden.hidden_relu_dead:.2f}}, @conv {{mechanism.q3.cifar10_h128_lr0.02.tanh+relu@conv.hidden_relu_dead:.2f}}; the conv layer itself stays
mostly alive (ReLU {{mechanism.q3.cifar10_h128_lr0.02.relu.conv_relu_dead:.3f}}). Mixing tanh into the conv layer goes with a living hidden
layer; whether bounding the conv output is the cause is a Part B test.

**Q4. Leaky-ReLU weight explosion.** Stage 0 mlp2 H128 LR 0.03 [E-S0]: {{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.n_spike}}/{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.n_spike:n}} runs spike; the
output-layer weight norm grows by a median factor {{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.jump_output_med:.3g}} in one epoch (epochs
{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.spike_epoch_min:.0f}}-{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.spike_epoch_max:.0f}}); logit spread across inputs at the spike {{report.q4.s0_mnist_mlp2_lr0.03.lbs_at:.2g}}; max softmax
probability {{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.maxprob_at_med:.2f}}; at most {{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.03.leaky_dead_max:.3f}} of units dead. The jump grows with LR
(×{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.02.jump_output_med:.2g}} at 0.02, ×{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.05.jump_output_med:.2g}} at 0.05) and the spike comes earlier (epochs
{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.02.spike_epoch_min:.0f}}-{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.02.spike_epoch_max:.0f}} vs {{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.05.spike_epoch_min:.0f}}-{{mechanism.q4.s0_h128_lr0.05.spike_epoch_max:.0f}}). Within an (H, LR) cell the spike epoch hardly varies: ICC
{{mechanism.q4.spread.s0_mnist_mlp2.icc:.3f}} (S0 mlp2), {{mechanism.q4.spread.s2_mnist_cfg1.icc:.3f}} / {{mechanism.q4.spread.s2_mnist_cfg2.icc:.3f}} (MNIST cfg1 / cfg2), {{mechanism.q4.spread.s2_cifar10_cfg1.icc:.2f}} /
{{mechanism.q4.spread.s2_cifar10_cfg2.icc:.2f}} (CIFAR-10). No single pre-spike quantity is constant across cells (S0 coefficient of
variation: hidden1 weight norm {{mechanism.q4.pred.s0_mnist_mlp2.w_hidden1_at_spike-1.cv_all:.2f}}, LR × output w² {{mechanism.q4.pred.s0_mnist_mlp2.lr_w_output2_at_spike-1.cv_all:.1f}}). After the spike the run
sits at the plateau: S0 LR 0.03 validation {{mechanism.q4.recovery.s0_mnist_mlp2_lr0.03.val_before:.1f}} % before, {{mechanism.q4.recovery.s0_mnist_mlp2_lr0.03.val_at:.1f}} % at the spike,
{{mechanism.q4.recovery.s0_mnist_mlp2_lr0.03.val_final:.1f}} % final. The plateau is mlp2-specific: MNIST cfg1 LR 0.02 recovers to {{mechanism.q4.recovery.s2_mnist_cfg1_lr0.02.val_final:.1f}} %
and CIFAR-10 cfg1 LR 0.02 ends at {{mechanism.q4.recovery.s2_cifar10_cfg1_lr0.02.val_final:.1f}} % [D]. The training loss after the spike equals
the clamp value times the training error rate: over {{mechanism.q4.clamp.n_runs}} spiked runs and {{mechanism.q4.clamp.n_epochs}}
post-spike epochs, |loss / (27.63 × error) − 1| ≤ {{mechanism.q4.clamp.max_abs_dev:.3f}}.

**Q5. Partial collapse.** late_degradation runs ending below 50 %: Stage 0 {{mechanism.q5.n_partial_runs_s0}}, Stage 2
{{mechanism.q5.n_partial_runs_s2}}, Stage 3 {{mechanism.q5.n_partial_runs_s3}} (`q5_partial_collapse.csv`: predicted classes and surviving units per
layer).

**Q6. Early warning.** ROC AUC of a signal at epoch e for "failure in e+1..e+3" (negatives:
epochs of stable runs of the same cell): loss rise {{mechanism.q6.s0.loss_rise.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s2.loss_rise.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s3.loss_rise.auc:.2f}}
(S0 / S2 / S3), max |z| jump {{mechanism.q6.s0.zmax_jump.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s2.zmax_jump.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s3.zmax_jump.auc:.2f}}, dead fraction > 20 %
{{mechanism.q6.s0.dead_gt20.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s2.dead_gt20.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s3.dead_gt20.auc:.2f}}, dw spike {{mechanism.q6.s0.dw_spike.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s2.dw_spike.auc:.2f}} / {{mechanism.q6.s3.dw_spike.auc:.2f}}.
The best S0 signal (dw spike) fires ≥ 1 epoch before failure in {{mechanism.q6.s0.dw_spike.n_lead_ge1}} of {{mechanism.q6.s0.dw_spike.n_lead_ge1:n}} failing
runs. No signal warns reliably.

**Depth.** Late collapse after learning in pure ReLU needs two ReLU layers (mlp2, or conv +
hidden). mlp1 ReLU never collapses late: MNIST {{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.mnist.mlp1.relu.n_late_collapse}}/{{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.mnist.mlp1.relu.n_late_collapse:n}}, CIFAR-10
{{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.cifar10.mlp1.relu.n_late_collapse}}/{{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.cifar10.mlp1.relu.n_late_collapse:n}} Stage 2 runs; CIFAR-10 mlp1 ReLU instead never learns
({{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.cifar10.mlp1.relu.n_never_learned}}/{{outcomes.depth.v6_stage2.cifar10.mlp1.relu.n_never_learned:n}} runs; every one of its final < 15 % runs at H128 is never_learned, share
{{critical_lr.ratio.v6_stage2.cifar10.mlp1.h128.fail.nl_share_relu:.2f}}). Matched at LR 0.02 [D]: CIFAR-10 CNN ReLU late_collapse {{report.depth_lr0.02.cifar10.cnn_late_collapse}}, mlp1
late_collapse {{report.depth_lr0.02.cifar10.mlp1_late_collapse}} and never_learned {{report.depth_lr0.02.cifar10.mlp1_never_learned}}. Across all mlp1 runs (Stages 1-2),
{{outcomes.depth.mlp1.n_late_collapse}} meet the late_collapse rule, none of them pure ReLU ({{outcomes.depth.mlp1.late_collapse_models}}; {{outcomes.depth.mlp1.late_collapse_datasets}};
best ≤ {{outcomes.depth.mlp1.late_collapse_best_max:.1f}} %, final {{outcomes.depth.mlp1.late_collapse_final_min:.1f}}-{{outcomes.depth.mlp1.late_collapse_final_max:.1f}} %): near-chance degradations of weakly
trained runs, not the dead-layer collapse. The data support: *late collapse of pure ReLU
networks occurs with two ReLU layers on both datasets and never with one; with one layer,
high LR either degrades (MNIST) or prevents learning (CIFAR-10).*

